<title>USA: Stratus Computer cuts memory, system prices.</title>
<headline>Stratus Computer cuts memory, system prices.</headline>
<dateline>MARLBORO, Mass. 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stratus Computer Inc said Monday it has reduced prices for memory and system packages for its Continuum line of systems.</p>
<p>Memory prices are being cut by 32 percent to $95 a megabyte from $140 a megabyte. Prices for packaged systems are being reduced by up to 17 percent for configurations with large memory.</p>
<p>The company did not offer price ranges for its packaged systems affected by the reduction.</p>
</text>
